{"id":"resp_bb40255e6b3efc1d","created_at":1795618494,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_a8a22d72e415be99","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to generate SHACL shape for requirement TRF-128: compressor charge time constraint, with condition based on ice class IA Super and propulsionEngineReversalRequiredForAstern.\n\nWe have term owners: compressorChargeTime applies to ship. iceClass also applies to ship. propulsionEngineReversalRequiredForAstern applies to ship.\n\nWe need shape targeting ships (class ship). Use sh:targetClass <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship>. Define properties: compressorChargeTime must be a QuantityValue with unit HR. Use qudt:QuantityValue class? According to quantityEncoding, quantity_class is http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue. Use property sh:property with path to compressorChargeTime. Add constraint: sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI? Actually value should be a QuantityValue node with numeric value and unit. Use sh:class qudt:QuantityValue.\n\nAlso need conditional constraint: If iceClass = iceClassIaSuper and propulsionEngineReversalRequiredForAstern = true then max charge time = 0.5 hour else <=1 hour.\n\nRepresent using sh:ifThen sh:if -> shape condition, sh:then -> shape constraint. In SHACL, we can use sh:property with sh:or? But best: Use sh:and with sh:if and sh:then? SHACL provides sh:if and sh:then in SPARQL? Actually SHACL Conditional (sh:condition) is in SHACL Advanced? There is sh:if and sh:then (since SHACL 1.1). Use sh:if with a shape that checks condition, and sh:then with shape constraining property.\n\nSo define a shape :CompressorChargeTimeShape with targetClass ship. Within, define sh:property for compressorChargeTime with sh:datatype xsd:decimal? But we're using QuantityValue node, so we may need to check numeric value.\n\nSimplify: Use sh:property path compressorChargeTime, sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI with sh:class qudt:QuantityValue, and then use sh:sparql constraint to enforce max.\n\nBut use sh:sparql to compute max based on condition.\n\nDefine a sh:node shape for ship that includes optional properties iceClass and propulsionEngineReversalRequiredForAstern.\n\nShacl conditional:\n\n:ShipShape a sh:NodeShape ;\n   sh:targetClass vocab:ship ;\n   sh:property [\n     sh:path vocab:compressorChargeTime ;\n     sh:class qudt:QuantityValue ;\n   ] ;\n   sh:if [\n     sh:and (\n        [ sh:path vocab:iceClass ; sh:hasValue vocab:iceClassIaSuper ]\n        [ sh:path vocab:propulsionEngineReversalRequiredForAstern ; sh:hasValue true^^xsd:boolean ]\n     )\n   ] ;\n   sh:then [\n     sh:property [\n        sh:path vocab:compressorChargeTime ;\n        sh:property [\n           sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n           sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n           sh:maxInclusive 0.5 ;\n        ] ;\n        sh:property [\n           sh:path qudt:unit ;\n           sh:hasValue <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HR> ;\n        ] ;\n     ] ;\n   ] ;\n   sh:else [\n     sh:property [\n        sh:path vocab:compressorChargeTime ;\n        sh:property [\n           sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n           sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n           sh:maxInclusive 1 ;\n        ] ;\n        sh:property [\n           sh:path qudt:unit ;\n           sh:hasValue <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HR> ;\n        ] ;\n     ] ;\n   ] .\n\nBut SHACL doesn't have sh:else; only sh:if and sh:then. For else, we can define a separate shape with sh:not of condition? Simpler: define two shapes with sh:targetClass ship, one with sh:if condition and then max 0.5, another with sh:not sh:if? Use sh:property with sh:maxCount? Could use sh:sparql property shape to compute.\n\nMaybe use sh:rule? Probably simpler via sh:sparqlConstraint.\n\nDefine a shape with a SPARQL constraint:\n\nsh:sparql [\n   a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;\n   sh:message \"Compressor charge time must be <= 0.5 h for IA Super ships with reversal required.\" ;\n   sh:select \"\"\"\n      SELECT $this ( ?value ) WHERE {\n        $this vocab:compressorChargeTime ?qt .\n        ?qt qudt:numericValue ?val .\n        ?qt qudt:unit <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HR> .\n        $this vocab:iceClass vocab:iceClassIaSuper .\n        $this vocab:propulsionEngineReversalRequiredForAstern true .\n        FILTER(?val > 0.5)\n      }\n   \"\"\" ;\n] .\n\nSimilarly another constraint for other ships: ensure <=1.\n\nBut that may double count; but both fire; if first ship doesn't meet condition, no violation, second may still trigger if >1.\n\nSecond constraint catches all ships regardless of class? Need to enforce <=1 for all ships, and the tighter <=0.5 for IA Super with reversal. So two constraints: universal <=1, and conditional <=0.5.\n\nImplement both.\n\nThus shape:\n\n:ShipCompressorShape a sh:NodeShape ;\n   sh:targetClass vocab:ship ;\n   sh:sparql [\n      a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;\n      sh:message \"Compressor charge time must not exceed 1 hour.\" ;\n      sh:select \"\"\"\n        SELECT $this WHERE {\n          $this vocab:compressorChargeTime ?qt .\n          ?qt qudt:numericValue ?val .\n          ?qt qudt:unit <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HR> .\n          FILTER(?val > 1)\n        }\n      \"\"\" ;\n   ] ;\n   sh:sparql [\n      a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;\n      sh:message \"Compressor charge time must not exceed 0.5 hour for IA Super ships requiring reversal.\" ;\n      sh:select \"\"\"\n        SELECT $this WHERE {\n          $this vocab:compressorChargeTime ?qt .\n          ?qt qudt:numericValue ?val .\n          ?qt qudt:unit <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HR> .\n          $this vocab:iceClass vocab:iceClassIaSuper .\n          $this vocab:propulsionEngineReversalRequiredForAstern true .\n          FILTER(?val > 0.5)\n        }\n      \"\"\" ;\n   ] .\n\nNeed prefixes.\n\nAlso ensure that compressorChargeTime exists? Not required, but maybe we add sh:property with sh:minCount 1? Not in requirement; only capacity must be sufficient, implying existence. Could enforce existence across all ships: sh:minCount 1 for that property. Use sh:property.\n\nDefine sh:property with path vocab:compressorChargeTime, sh:minCount 1, sh:class qudt:QuantityValue.\n\nAdd unit consistent: we can also enforce unit via sh:property on the quantity node, but SPARQL already checks unit.\n\nImplement.\n\nNow produce output with <BEGIN_SHACL> line then Turtle.","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_8b4cc6a51768aaea","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix vocab: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt#> .\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n\n# Shape targeting all ships\n:vesselCompressorShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass vocab:ship ;\n    \n    # The ship must have a compressorChargeTime value (QuantityValue)\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path vocab:compressorChargeTime ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:class qudt:QuantityValue ;\n    ] ;\n    \n    # Universal constraint: charge time must not exceed 1 hour\n    sh:sparql [\n        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;\n        sh:message \"Compressor charge time must not exceed 1 hour.\" ;\n        sh:select \"\"\"\n            SELECT $this WHERE {\n                $this vocab:compressorChargeTime ?qt .\n                ?qt qudt:numericValue ?val .\n                ?qt qudt:unit unit:HR .\n                FILTER(?val > 1)\n            }\n        \"\"\" ;\n    ] ;\n    \n    # Conditional tighter constraint for IA Super ships requiring reversal\n    sh:sparql [\n        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;\n        sh:message \"For IA Super ships that require propulsion reversal for astern, the compressor charge time must not exceed 0.5 hour.\" ;\n        sh:select \"\"\"\n            SELECT $this WHERE {\n                $this vocab:compressorChargeTime ?qt .\n                ?qt qudt:numericValue ?val .\n                ?qt qudt:unit unit:HR .\n                $this vocab:iceClass vocab:iceClassIaSuper .\n                $this vocab:propulsionEngineReversalRequiredForAstern true .\n                FILTER(?val > 0.5)\n            }\n        \"\"\" ;\n    ] .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":60240,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":592,"cache_write_tokens":59632,"input_tokens_per_turn":[60240],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[592]},"output_tokens":1996,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1523,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1996],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":62236},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}